From 9007e304eb411b3910cc082a1912f8a5c96ed947 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:44:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 088/240] Bugfix: validate vertex count and permutation values
 read by `orderLoad()` [report R. Perry]

`orderLoad()` replaced the vertex count of the ordering by the count
read from the file and used the latter as the loop bound while
reading into an array sized according to the former, so that a file
with a larger count overflowed the permutation array. Permutation
values were never range-checked before being used as indices by
`orderPeri()`, and duplicate values left holes in the inverse
permutation that crashed later computations.

Reject a count that differs from the number of vertices of the
ordering, check that each rank lies within [baseval, vnodnbr +
baseval[ and that it is not already assigned, and build the inverse
permutation on the fly, which removes the need for the temporary
direct permutation array. The vertex count of the ordering is no
longer modified by a failed load.

Add a save/load round trip and invalid ordering files (bad count,
out-of-range rank, duplicate rank) to test_scotch_graph_order.

Refs: GRA-03
